And that might be what “real-life quality rendering” ultimately means for this project—not photorealism.

Structural realism.

A representation rich enough that when we compress reality into it and unfold it again, the important causal and relational properties survive.

Which gives us another useful target:

Don’t make the Pantheon resemble reality. Make its compressed representations regenerate consequences that resemble reality.

The mosaic becomes convincing not when we can no longer see the tiles.

It becomes convincing when the light behaves correctly across them.